---
/* The staging area: one finding expanded, with the plain-words explanation. */
import MockFrame from "./MockFrame.astro";
---
<MockFrame label="finding · src/orders/cutoff.ts:142" right="Stale · 1 new commit">
  <div class="mk-card staged">
    <div class="mk-line">
      <span class="mk-check" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      <span class="status is-amber"><i aria-hidden="true"></i>Should fix</span>
      <span class="mk-title">Cut-off uses the server's clock, not the customer's</span>
      <span class="status is-green"><i aria-hidden="true"></i>Confirmed ×2</span>
    </div>
    <p class="why">A customer in Perth can miss the 5 pm cut-off at 2 pm because the comparison runs in UTC.</p>
    <details class="detail">
      <summary class="mk-dim">Technical detail</summary>
      <p class="mk-dim">isBeforeCutoff() compares Date.now() against a wall-clock hour with no zone. Every call site passes the customer's timezone already.</p>
    </details>
    <pre class="mk-code"><span class="mk-del">- const now = new Date();</span>
<span class="mk-add">+ const now = zonedNow(customer.timezone);</span>
  return now.getHours() &lt; CUTOFF_HOUR;</pre>
    <div class="mk-sub">
      <div class="mk-h"><b>Explain simply &amp; how to verify</b><span class="mk-dim">Your Claude</span></div>
      <p class="mk-dim simple">The order deadline is checked on the server's clock. For a shop in another timezone the deadline lands at the wrong hour.</p>
      <ol>
        <li>Set a customer's timezone to Australia/Perth.</li>
        <li>Place an order at 14:30 Perth time.</li>
        <li>Expected: accepted. Current: rejected as past cut-off.</li>
      </ol>
    </div>
    <div class="mk-foot">
      <span class="mk-dim">Original kept for the learnings loop.</span>
      <span class="mk-foot-actions"><span class="mk-btn">Edit</span><span class="mk-btn mk-btn-quiet">Drop</span></span>
    </div>
  </div>
</MockFrame>
<style>
  .staged { box-shadow: inset 3px 0 0 var(--blue); }
  .why { margin: 0; color: var(--graphite); }
  .detail summary { cursor: default; list-style: none; }
  .detail summary::before { content: "▸ "; }
  .detail p { margin: 0.3rem 0 0; }
  .simple { margin: 0; }
</style>
